          "name": "copy_all_text",
          "canonical_hash": "sha256:b57d84395c4d6c85fb6b5d9f45fb51bcf1c4353c48291ec75307da1ae2d789af",
          "description": "Read ALL text of the focused window / web page EXACTLY. Reads the document through accessibility first (no keystrokes, nothing selected); where that is unavailable, select-all + copy, then the clipboard is restored. Exact characters (IDs, amounts, codes) — prefer it over OCR for reading pages and documents. Refuses in terminals (Ctrl+C would interrupt them). Never presses select-all while focus is in an editable field, an editor document or a list — it returns the accessibility text then. After a select-all copy the content stays selected (the result says so); focus the right window first.",
